      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PASADENA (7) progressive gelding who indicated he was back in great shape with a slashing second from last on the turn in a tight finish over 1200m at Ballarat. Covered a stack of ground on that occasion and ready for the extra trip with the blinkers being added. Go close. CASHOUT (1) sharp gelding going quickly through the grades with the three wins this time in. Won by a big space again (4 lens) over 1400m at Cranbourne in BM74 class. Will sit on the speed and figure prominently. THEBELMONTGANGSTER (2) will find this more to his liking third up after he travelled wide throughout when thirteenth to Cross Tasman over 1400m in a solid rating BM88 at Randwick. Can stalk the speed and improve sharply. ROSE AYE (8) comes here with a fitness edge over most of these after fading in the Kosciuszko over 1200m at Randwick. Placed at the trip and keep safe.",
